# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# StageZero Environment Configuration
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to .env and update values for your environment
# DO NOT commit .env to source control

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# APPLICATION
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development

# HTTPS CERTIFICATE (Docker only)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Password for the HTTPS certificate (.volumes/https/aspnetapp.pfx)
# See .volumes/https/README.md for certificate setup instructions
CERT_PASSWORD=STRONG_PASSWORD

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EMAIL: NONE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# StageZero does not send email. A "forgot password" code is written to the
# application log (`docker logs <container>` in Docker) as a banner headed
# STAGEZERO PASSWORD RESET CODE. Nothing to configure.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CODELIFTER.NET SIGNUPS (OPTIONAL)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The first-run setup form offers two unchecked boxes: the CodeLifter newsletter
# and StageZero update news. Ticked, they post once to codelifter.net, which
# sends a single confirmation email. To hide the boxes entirely (a fork, an
# air-gapped install), set the URL to blank:
# CodeLifter__SubscriptionsUrl=

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CLOUDFLARE TUNNEL (OPTIONAL — DOCKER SIDECAR ONLY)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Only needed if you run the cloudflared connector as a container instead of a
# host service. Get the token from StageZero's Tunnel Setup page, then start the
# stack with:
#   docker compose -f prod.docker-compose.yml --profile tunnel up -d
#
# Running cloudflared as a host service (macOS launchd / Windows service /
# systemd) is the recommended setup — the connector then survives the app stack
# going down. See ..Documentation/CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_SETUP.md.
#
# Treat this like a password: it grants the ability to serve traffic on your
# tunnel's hostnames.
# TUNNEL_TOKEN=
